        "method": "csv row 195/234 sha256:e054cfc962805b78",
        "content": "# Accenture \u2014 Flowable\n\n## Lead record\n- **company**: Accenture\n- **tool**: Flowable\n- **priority**: 9 \u00b7 do not pitch\n- **geo**: IE Dublin / global\n- **principal**: \u2014\n- **email**: \u2014\n- **website**: accenture.com\n- **tool_url**: https://www.flowable.com/\n- **impressum_url**: \u2014\n- **contact_verified**: No\n- **headcount**: \u2014\n- **hq**: \u2014\n- **owner_parent**: \u2014\n- **tech_partners**: \u2014\n- **federation**: \u2014\n- **posture**: \u2014\n- **tier**: Do not pitch\n- **verdict**: \u2014\n- **flag**: 513,000 staff. Enterprise anti-persona (AP-2) \u2014 no procurement-track motion in this brief \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.\n- **source**: Flowable Partner Finder (mined 2026-08-18)\n- **powerhouse_fit**: Flowable orchestrates WHEN things happen \u2014 the process/case instance is a mutable row and history is purgeable. Same gap as Camunda, same seam: Powerhouse holds the append-only, user-attributed record of what was decided, and Flowable calls a Switchboard mutation at each decision point. Flowable's base is heavily banking/insurance, where 'who approved this, under which rule' is already a funded question.\n- **demo_scenario**: Flowable service task / event listener dispatching a typed operation at each user-task or case milestone. Then purge the Flowable instance and replay the approval chain from Powerhouse. A Camunda delegate and a Flowable listener are the same integration twice \u2014 build one, ship both.",
